drive-native (0.1.0~dev20261109.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge the #2/#6/#8/#9/#10/#11/#14/#18/#19/#50/#53 batch:
    - #14: park permission-uncertain uploads in an explicit local
      "abandoned" state once the five-attempt reconciliation budget is
      exhausted, offer AbandonUpload (token CAS, removes only the local
      unsent file, never a server entry), surface a paused_uploads counter,
      protect abandoned bodies from cache GC until an explicit retry
      re-arms them, and supersede residual pending uploads when a creation
      is abandoned or locally deleted.
    - #19: run cache release as a cancellable background job with per-file
      progress and exact reclaimed bytes, return skipped for already
      online-only entries while withdrawing their failed read intents, and
      let garbage collection drop dangling blob pointers of deleted nodes
      without touching bodies still referenced by live, conflicted or
      journaled rows; stop GUI polling when the service reports the job is
      gone.
    - #18: answer hard links with EOPNOTSUPP instead of EPERM so tools fall
      back to copy/rename; document that Synology Drive has no hard-link
      identity.
    - #53: refresh the overview whenever the committed status watermark
      advances so tray badges and navigation counts cannot go stale.
    - #8: prove the fourth acceptance criterion with a reproducible test
      (concurrent desktop reads during real initialization); no runtime
      behavior change.
    - #6 and #54: heal stale directory conflict flags after snapshot
      installs and successful mkdir/rename confirmations while keeping real
      conflicts, and add keep-local/keep-remote recovery for bound
      directories deleted by the server (conflict center and D-Bus actions).
    - #2: deliver problem notifications through freedesktop D-Bus when the
      tray is unavailable, route clicks to the originating mount, and keep
      the existing notification policy.
    - #50: add optional profile exclude_patterns (compiled regex, validated
      on save) whose subtrees are pruned from initialization, hidden from
      FUSE/GetDirectory/GetStates and events, and refused on local write and
      scheduling; switching rules locally hides and purges imported content
      and recycles blobs without deleting anything remotely, with restore on
      rule removal; fix preview-phase mounts with active rules; add a GUI
      rule editor.
    - #9: raise STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION to 29 with commit outcome/diagnostic
      columns, schema_migrations, recovery_runs, platform_state_changes and
      a commit_diagnostics view, plus idempotent backfill and a
      state-before-v29-* backup; persist commit diagnostics for the upload,
      rename, mkdir, remove and replace paths and expose additive
      GetOverview.commit_diagnostics, keeping IPC at 21.
    - #10: classify required-rebuild signals (rescan_later, merge_mode,
      snapshot/cursor gaps) separately from retryable and fatal errors,
      rebuild automatically with at most three backoff attempts, and expose
      an additive recovery status object; only authentication, certificate,
      root and exhaustion cases need attention.
    - #11 step 0/1: add a drive-core POSIX guard wired into verify.sh and
      the Windows port design, and introduce the FileIdentitySource
      contract behind a u64 platform id without changing schema, IPC or
      FUSE behavior.
  * v28 -> v29 is the only migration path; FSD and worker must be updated
    together and old programs cannot read the new schema. Store::open keeps
    a VACUUM INTO state-before-v29-* backup before migrating.

